 "attributes": {
  "title": {
   "en": "Telecaster B-Boy"
  },
  "altTitles": [
   {
    "ja": "テレキャスタービーボーイ"
   }
  ],
  "description": {
   "en": "Kaede Tsuki, a high school student who belongs to a light music club, is feeling bewildered by her inability to fit in with her surroundings and her own goals. One day, she attends her favorite band's concert for the first time and meets Asuka, a friend of her older sister. Asuka is attending a vocational school for nursery school, but she is unable to give up on her music career, which she once devoted herself to. Kaede Tsuki and Asuka were feeling suffocated in their stagnant daily lives. They hit it off and start a band, but various obstacles stand in their way. Friends, family, adults, people you love. People try to understand someone. We want someone to understand us.\nIn the process, they discover a little bit of themselves that they can like.",
   "ja": "軽音部に所属する高校2年生の風間楓月（かざまかづき）は、 クラスメイトとは違う自分の価値観や趣味嗜好、自分自身の在り方に悩んでいた。 そんなある日、大好きなバンド「ハジマリノハナシ」のライブをきっかけに 姉の友人である花山飛鳥（はなやまあすか）と出会い、楓月の世界は少しずつ変化していく―—。  誰かを理解したい、誰かに理解されたいともがく中で ちょっと好きになれる自分を見つけ出す青春ストーリー!!"
  },
